From: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: vt-sbc-am62l: soft-start the backlight boost, panel up dark

The backlight boost draws about 0.5 A for a millisecond when its enable
is driven with a plain edge from cold. With the kernel default brightness
at 100, pwm-backlight enables it the instant the panel driver reports
display-on, on top of the panel's own surge: the feed reaches ~0.73 A,
the input stage trips at ~4.1 V board-side (5 V through 5 m of cable) and
the board reboots at 1.4 s. Measured with a Joulescope on the feed: the
panel alone peaks at ~0.55 A and survives; the two together do not.

Soft-start the enable (400 x 50 us ramp, regulator-fixed) and bring the
panel up dark; backlight-boot.service raises it to the product level once
psplash has drawn, through the ramp, when nothing else is switching.

Signed-off-by: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/vt-sbc-am62l.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/vt-sbc-am62l.dtsi
@@ -63,6 +63,15 @@
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		enable-active-high;
+		/*
+		 * Backlight boost: ~0.5 A cold inrush when enabled with a plain
+		 * edge, which on a 5 V feed through a long cable trips the
+		 * input stage if it lands on the panel's display-on surge.
+		 * Ramped enable (see regulator-fixed), pad pulled down so the
+		 * boost is off until the kernel enables it.
+		 */
+		vantron,soft-start-pulses = <400>;
+		vantron,soft-start-period-us = <50>;
 		gpio = <&main_gpio0 91 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&backlight_pins_default>;
@@ -206,7 +215,14 @@
 			240 241 242 243 244 245 246 247
 			248 249 250 251 252 253 254 255
 		>;
-		default-brightness-level = <100>;
+		/*
+		 * 0: the panel comes up dark. backlight-boot.service (recipes-
+		 * graphics/display-rotation) raises it to the product level once
+		 * the panel is on and the boot's probe storm is over, through the
+		 * ramped enable above, so the boost's inrush never coincides with
+		 * display-on.
+		 */
+		default-brightness-level = <0>;
 	};
 	watchdog_gpio: watchdog-gpio {
 		compatible ="linux,wdt-gpio";
@@ -724,7 +740,7 @@
 	};
 	backlight_pins_default: backlight-default-pins {
 		pinctrl-single,pins = <
-			AM62LX_IOPAD(0x01b0, PIN_INPUT, 7) /* (B12) SPI0_D1.GPIO0_91 */
+			AM62LX_IOPAD(0x01b0, PIN_INPUT_PULLDOWN, 7) /* (B12) SPI0_D1.GPIO0_91 */
 		>;
 		bootph-all;
 	};
